  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nSurface high pressure will remain in place across the region through\ntonight. This will result in mostly clear conditions and continued \nsomewhat below normal temperatures. Highs today will be in the upper\n70s to lower 80s. The surface high will shift off the east through \nthe day on Wednesday. In return flow, temperatures will moderate \nsomewhat with highs in the low to mid 80s. \n\nA weak mid level short wave will move across the southern Great Lakes\nWednesday night into Thursday. This will help push an associated \nweak cold front into our area through the day on Thursday. Ahead of \nthe short wave, showers and thunderstorms will likely develop off to \nour northwest during the day on Wednesday, with some of this activity\nmoving into our area from the northwest Wednesday evening/night, but\nlikely weakening as it does. Additional chances for showers and \nthunderstorms will then develop through the day on Thursday as we \ndestabilize through the afternoon and the front approaches from the \nnorthwest. Deep layer shear does begin to increase a bit through \nThursday afternoon so suppose a few stronger storms may be possible \nduring the afternoon into early evening.",
